From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:32:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 89/89] web-app: reactions bar inside the message context menu

Reacting took two steps (right-click, "React", then a separate bar) or a
hover icon. Signal and Telegram put the reactions on top of the message
menu; do the same.

ContextMenu gains an optional `header` component, rendered inside the
modal <dialog> (anything outside it is inert while the menu is open) and
positioned with the menu as one block. Keyboard: the header's own roving
tabindex handles left/right, ArrowDown enters the menu, ArrowUp on the
first item returns to the header. Message passes the ReactionsBar as the
header and drops the "React" item; "more emojis" closes the menu and
hands over to the standalone bar with the picker open, which already
keeps the large picker on screen. Ctrl/Cmd+R is unchanged.

The hover react / "..." icons are gone and no column is reserved for
them. "..." stays in the DOM, visually hidden until :focus-visible, so
keyboard users keep a focusable way in (macOS has no Menu key); Enter on
the focused message itself (not on a link or media control inside it)
opens the menu as well. The saved-messages "show in chat" button stays.

The long-press fallback (0079) still leaves selectable text to text
selection, but a press on a link now opens the menu (Copy Link), with
-webkit-touch-callout off on message links so iOS's preview sheet does
not cover it.
